// Tests run on node (node:test, native type stripping) but drive the worker,
// so they are typechecked against the SAME lib the worker targets: the
// @cloudflare/workers-types inherited from tsconfig.json, not node's.
//
// That matters because the integration tests import all of src/. Adding
// `types: ["node"]` here would typecheck the Workers-runtime modules against
// node's globals too, where `Response`/`Headers` are undici's and `json()`
// returns `unknown` — src would have to be contorted to satisfy two conflicting
// definitions of the same global. Node's own APIs are still available: they are
// reached through explicit `node:*` module imports (node:test, node:http,
// node:buffer), which resolve without putting node's globals in scope.
{
	"extends": "./tsconfig.json",
	"compilerOptions": {
		"allowImportingTsExtensions": true
	},
	"include": ["tests/**/*"]
}
